@startuml
!theme cyborg
skinparam backgroundColor #111827
skinparam defaultFontColor #F3F4F6
title Proposed — Guarded write and post-commit cache coherence
skinparam backgroundColor #111827
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

actor Caller
participant "Owner handler" as H
database "Authoritative local state" as D
participant "Optional derived cache" as C
Caller -> H : exact intent + identity + expected version
H -> D : guarded current authority/version/invariant admission
alt denied / conflict / invalid
 D --> H : no admitted mutation; safe refusal
else eligible new or duplicate intent
 H -> D : coherent owned writes + attributable command result\nplus durable invalidation intent if actually needed
 D --> H : committed result or uncertain observation
 opt actual commit established and cache exists
  H -> C : invalidate / advance exact version after commit
  C --> H : actual invalidation outcome, possibly unavailable
 end
 H --> Caller : actual committed / unresolved outcome
end
note over H,C
 Lost invalidation must not allow stale private authority/content delivery.
 Every read uses current version/eligibility or evaluated atomic coherence.
 Cache failure after commit is not database rollback.
end note

@enduml